From 755591361bee045e490057ffeb8a858a792169dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 16:22:02 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] common: add the native AROS system utility backend

AI_PHASE: Phase 3 - single-process headless shell

AI_STATUS: ANGLE common now supplies explicit AROS path, environment, timer, thread, native-library, and fail-closed memory/debug contracts.

ROOT_CAUSE: ANGLE_PLATFORM_POSIX selected portable compiler primitives, but libGLESv2.gni only added system utility implementations for Linux-family, Apple, Windows, Fuchsia, and Android targets. AROS therefore linked no implementation at all.

FIX_REASON: Add an AROS-owned backend instead of compiling Linux dlopen, procfs, and signal assumptions. Use debug.library for unsupported-operation diagnostics and return failure for contracts AROS does not yet implement.

SCOPE: third_party/angle BUILD.gn, src/libGLESv2.gni, and src/common/system_utils_aros.cpp

VALIDATION: ninja -C out/aros-headless -j4 obj/third_party/angle/angle_common/system_utils_aros.o passed; a focused libGLESv2.so link eliminated all ANGLE platform-helper undefined symbols and now stops only at the independent AROS startup.o/main shared-link issue.

RISK: Dynamic symbol lookup and MMU page protection remain deliberately unsupported; static ANGLE Phase 3 does not require them, and later native GPU/dynamic-library phases must replace these fail-closed paths.

AI_DECISION_CHAIN: ACD-chromium-native-port-roadmap
